# ==============================================================================
# EmailJS Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# 1. Create a free account at https://www.emailjs.com/
# 2. Add an Email Service (e.g., Gmail) -> Copy the Service ID (e.g., service_xxxxxxx)
# 3. Create an Email Template -> Copy the Template ID (e.g., template_xxxxxxx)
#    Available template parameters sent by all forms:
#    - {{name}} / {{from_name}} (Sender name)
#    - {{email}} / {{reply_to}} (Sender email address)
#    - {{phone}} (Sender phone number or "Not provided")
#    - {{subject}} (Email subject line)
#    - {{message}} (Formatted message body)
#    - {{to_name}} (Recipient name)
#    - {{recipient_email}} (Recipient email)
#    - {{submission_time}} (Timestamp of submission)
# 4. In Account -> General -> Copy your Public Key (e.g., xxxxxxx_xxxxxxx)
# 5. In Account -> Security -> Allowed Origins:
#    Ensure your live Vercel domain (e.g., https://your-portfolio.vercel.app)
#    and localhost (http://localhost:5173) are allowed, or leave blank if unrestricted.
#
# LOCALHOST DEVELOPMENT:
# Copy this file to `.env` in the project root and fill in your values.
#
# VERCEL PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT:
# 1. Go to your Vercel Project Dashboard -> Settings -> Environment Variables.
# 2. Add each of these 3 variables for Production (and Preview/Development):
#    - VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID
#    - VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID
#    - VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY
# 3. Trigger a Redeploy (Deployments -> ... -> Redeploy) so Vite embeds them at build time.
# ==============================================================================

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id_here
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id_here
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key_here
